RF.put("questb:b39",{"8439":{"id":8439,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"92519":{"id":92519,"t":"Ward restocking","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Pick up a case of Packaged Tonics at Jorell's lab in Go'shek Farm and return to Doctor Gregory Victor in Hammerfall.\nPackaged Tonics","desc":"Apothecary Jorell was supposed to bring us a case of antidotes and elixirs days ago, but we're still empty handed. That fool has probably poisoned himself again by brewing in that poorly-ventilated shack he calls his lab.\nIf you want to further help our ward, you would be a far more reliable individual for this job.\nFollow the road to Go'shek farm, south and a bit west of here. You'll likely find it packed and ready to go, with Jorell either missing or unconcerned with his obligations.\nLevel 36 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 32 34 39 46 Side Horde Quest ID 92519\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 36, 5,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 36 ] Silky Sutures\nReturn 12 Surgical Spidersilk to Doctor Gregory Victor in Hammerfall, Arathi Highlands.\nDoctor Gregory Victor Arathi Highlands\n2,800 XP\n2 [ 36 ] Ward Restocking this quest\nPick up a case of Packaged Tonics at Jorell's lab in Go'shek Farm and return to Doctor Gregory Victor in Hammerfall.\n2,800 XP","cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"679":{"id":679,"t":"Call to Arms","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Mindslicer.","obj":"Kill 7 Boulderfist Shaman and 3 Boulderfist Lords and return to Drum Fel in the Hammerfall outpost.\nBoulderfist Shaman slain : 0/ 7\nBoulderfist Lord slain : 0/ 3","desc":"The head of the beast is ready to be taken off... with great force, ‹name›. You have shown every sign that you are able to help us with this final mighty blow. The leaders of these attacks have made their lair within the ruins of Stromgarde, a glaring symbol of human frailty.\nFind and slay those Boulderfist lords and their lackey shaman who would try and drive us from these lands.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSilent Hunter Skullsplitter Mindslicer\nNew in Forever: Mindslicer.\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I see your courage finally wanes. It seems my instincts were correct about you: your strength is nothing compared to your bravado.\nReturn to me when the beast's head has been severed, or return never again.","done":"You do your people proud, ‹name›. The threat has been greatly lessened, and I am sure we will begin to thrive here in the Highlands.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.2,"y":33.9,"n":"Drum Fel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"2759":{"id":2759,"t":"In Search of Galvan","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,550 experience instead of 2,200, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Speak with McGavan in Booty Bay.\nMithril Insignia\nProvided: Mithril Insignia","desc":"Although Galvan left Booty Bay many years ago, members of the order still remain in town, hoping to one day find another worthy of Galvan's tutelage.\nTake this insignia and present it to McGavan in Booty Bay.\nIf you actually make it that far, he'll know that you are worthy. I have faith, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 1,550","back":"A rare breed your kind be, matey. Let me see that insignia.","done":"By Blackhoof's back hair -- finally, one worthy of the Mithril Order!\nStormwind City Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.9,"y":36.8,"n":"Hank the Hammer","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.9,"y":75.4,"n":"McGavan","e":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97959":{"id":97959,"t":"Camping 101 mining","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Brom Killian in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your mining skill to 20","desc":"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","back":"You've come to learn, then?","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":56,"y":37,"n":"Brom Killian","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94359":{"id":94359,"t":"Craftsmans writ ghostweave vest","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Ghostweave Vest\nGhostweave Vest","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Ghostweave Vest, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Ghostweave Vest Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94359","cats":["crafting"]},"94279":{"id":94279,"t":"Craftsmans writ heavy mithril axe","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Heavy Mithril Axe\nHeavy Mithril Axe","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Heavy Mithril Axe, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Heavy Mithril Axe Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94279","cats":["crafting"]},"2519":{"id":2519,"t":"The Temple of the Moon","lv":10,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Sister Aquinne wants you to speak with Priestess A'moora in the Temple of the Moon.","desc":"A once great creature of the forest is in need of help, ‹race›.\nThere is a difficult task that must be done.\nPlease seek out Priestess A'moora; she will explain things to you. Find her to the southeast of here, inside the Temple of the Moon.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"So, Sister Aquinne sent you?","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":28.9,"y":45.8,"n":"Sister Aquinne","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":36.7,"y":85.9,"n":"Priestess A'moora","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"7799":{"id":7799,"t":"A Donation of Mageweave","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Mageweave Cloth Northshire Guard 54.5 % , Deep Dweller 48.4 % , Refuge Pointe Defender 40.7 % , Stonard Hunter 40.2 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Mageweave is running low, and we could use your help to replenish our stocks! By counting on the community as a whole, we would only need a donation of 60 pieces of mageweave cloth from you to enable us to reach our goal. Such generosity would not go unnoticed Darnassus, I assure you!\nIf you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":64,"y":23,"n":"Raedon Duskstriker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"99159":{"id":99159,"t":"Finding warmth","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 14 pieces of firewood.\n14 Mostly Dry Firewood","desc":"My hearth is open to warm any soul, but I'd like to ask you to help me if you could.\nI simply need more firewood. It is something I would normally do myself, but I have been preoccupied by other tasks.","back":"Light guide you on your tasks.","done":"Ah, perfect. These will do--any that are too wet to use right now I will leave to dry.\nNow, if you're willing, I have more tasks I could use help with.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Father Gavin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"1319":{"id":1319,"t":"The Black Shield","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Show the Blackened Iron Shield to Caz Twosprocket in Theramore.\nBlackened Iron Shield\nProvided: Blackened Iron Shield","desc":"I'm sorry I can't be of much help, ‹name›, but I can refer you to someone who would be. Caz Twosprocket, one of our best blacksmiths, works the forge at the smithy.\nTake the shield to him, and see what he can tell you.","rew":"Experience: 280","back":"Something for me to look at?","done":"Hm... interesting piece of iron you have here. Definitely not made by any of the blacksmiths I know over on this side of the sea, and it's certainly not my work.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":64.8,"y":50.4,"n":"Caz Twosprocket","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"1239":{"id":1239,"t":"The Severed Head","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Defiant Orc Head to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.\nDefiant Orc Head\nProvided: Defiant Orc Head","desc":"Vigorous digging reveals the head of a male orc, raggedly severed at the neck. His lips are frozen in a snarl, and its dark eyes stare defiantly.","rew":"Experience: 2,050\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You have another matter to report, ‹name›?","done":"This is the head of Marg Nighteye! As I feared, he is dead.\nLook at the wound on his neck! Could a weapon have made that ragged cut, or did some beast slay our agent?\nThis is a mystery we must solve, ‹name›. We must discover if Marg's death was at the hands of the Alliance!","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":55.4,"y":25.9,"n":"Loose Dirt","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":35.2,"y":30.7,"n":"Nazeer Bloodpike","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"39":{"id":39,"t":"Deliver Thomas' Report","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.","desc":"Tell Marshal Dughan of Malakai and Rolf's deaths, and report to him that the Murlocs in eastern Elwynn cannot be contained by our current troop presence.\nI know we don't have many troops to spare, but hopefully Dughan can find someone.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Hmm, this news is troubling. Already our defenses are stretched thin, and losing Rolf and Malakai to those murlocs put us in an even worse position.\nIf things don't improve, there will be fighting in Goldshire by the week's end!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":74,"y":72.2,"n":"Guard Thomas","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"1559":{"id":1559,"t":"Flash Bomb Recipe","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSchematic: Flash Bomb","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":42.4,"y":52.9,"n":"Rigglefuzz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"3639":{"id":3639,"t":"Show Your Work","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Big Iron Bombs, 20 Solid Dynamite, and 5 Explosive Sheep to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan.\n20 Big Iron Bomb\n20 Solid Dynamite\n5 Explosive Sheep sold by Kimberly Hiett","desc":"As your mentor, I want samples of your work. You're a skilled engineer; there is no question of this, ‹name›. What I hope to do though is analyze them for ways to emphasize goblin-oriented techniques in your future efforts. I need the following: twenty big iron bombs, twenty sticks of solid dynamite, and five explosive sheep - and keep the safeties armed!\nSubmit these items to me and I will issue you your own Goblin Engineer Membership Card; it is required for access to all goblin engineering trainers!","rew":"You will receive:\nGoblin Engineer Membership Card\nYou will learn: Goblin Engineer\nExperience: 3,150\n+75 reputation with Engineering - Goblin","back":"Once I receive your crafted engineering items for my review, I will hand you a genuine Goblin Engineer Membership Card! So long as the card is valid, you will have unlimited access to any goblin engineer trainer anywhere in the world.","done":"Here is your first Goblin Engineer Membership Card!\nThis card has its dues paid for in advance for fourteen days; all cards expire after two weeks of activity. When it does, pay your next set of dues to any goblin engineer trainer in order to get another card; without the card, your membership will temporarily lapse and you cannot access new schemata.\nThis never affects what you already know; once a goblin engineer, always a goblin engineer.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.3,"n":"Nixx Sprocketspring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"5159":{"id":5159,"t":"Cleansed Water Returns to Felwood","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Purified Moon Well Water to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.\nPurified Moonwell Water\nProvided: Purified Moonwell Water","desc":"Thank the spirits, ‹name›. They are the ones that have come to your aid, not me.\nI give this purified water to you now. Please give my regards to Greta and my best wishes. She is tackling something greater than many of us... as I'm sure she will soon find out.\nThe Shadow Council is not a force to be trifled with, ‹name›. Remember that.\nGo now. Take the water and return to Greta.","rew":"Experience: 2,700","back":"Ah, I see you've returned, ‹name›. Good. Did you find Islen in the Barrens? Or do we have to find another way to accomplish our goals?","done":"This should be more than enough water for our purposes.\nI'm glad to hear that Islen was able to help us. Her strength with the water spirits has always been a strong one. She is also wise, and rare is it that the spirits do not agree with her purpose. The fact that both of them have blessed our task gives me hope that we are on the right path.\nThe Barrens Felwood","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":51.2,"y":82.1,"n":"Greta Mosshoof","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4119":{"id":4119,"t":"Corrupted Night Dragon","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a night dragon plant. The fruits that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 4 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Night Dragon. It immediately begins to shed it's corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":40.7,"y":78.3,"n":"Corrupted Night Dragon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"519":{"id":519,"t":"The Crown of Will","lv":41,"min":34,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Targ, Muckrake, and Glommus and bring their heads to Melisara in Tarren Mill.\nTarg's Head Targ\nMuckrake's Head Muckrake\nGlommus's Head Glommus","desc":"Targ, Muckrake, and Glommus are Mug'Thol's lieutenants. They are loyal to him, though who can say what drives an ogre to loyalty.\nBring me their heads, ‹name›, and then all that will remain is to remove Mug'Thol's head, crown and all.","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I want their heads, ‹name›, not excuses.","done":"...and I thought ogres smelled foul enough to begin with.\nWhen you bring me Mug'Thol's head, I will have the four of them mounted on pikes above Alterac. A fitting monument to those who go against the Dark Lady's wishes.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.6,"y":20.6,"n":"Melisara","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"2039":{"id":2039,"t":"Find Bingles","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Bingles Blastenheimer in Loch Modan.","desc":"We've lost contact with Bingles! He was sent on a reconnaissance mission over Gnomeregan and hasn't reported back in over a week. I just know he's gone and blown himself up.\nHe was last seen flying over the Loch. Perhaps you can investigate, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 270\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"So Gnoarn doesn't trust my reconnaissance abilities? I wonder why...\nNevermind that, I need your assistance! Nay! The movement needs your assistance!\nDun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Gnoarn","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":63.6,"y":47.9,"n":"Bingles Blastenheimer","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2439":{"id":2439,"t":"The Platinum Discs","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take your reward voucher to Dinita Stonemantle in the Vault of Ironforge.\nReward Voucher\nProvided: Reward Voucher","desc":"This object is an incredible find. The ancient Titans, or the Creators as these discs refer to them as, are the link to our enchanted creation, if the lore stored in here is correct! We'll need to invest as much research time into this as possible.\nAs for you, heroic ‹class›, take this voucher to Dinita Stonemantle at the vault. It grants you what I think is a fitting for such a tremendous find!\nReturn to me directly when you are ready; there is much more to do for the Explorers' League!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Superior Healing Potion 5 Greater Mana Potion\nYou will also receive:\nThawpelt Sack\nExperience: 420","back":"Welcome to the Vault of Ironforge, ‹name›. What may I do for you today?","done":"As yes, a voucher from the Explorers' League... and quite the valuable one, might I add.\nThe Explorers' League lends me the authority to offer you a choice in your compensation directly from their vault. You are to receive this item, and you may choose between five superior healing potions or five greater mana potions as your reward.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":24.1,"n":"High Explorer Magellas","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":30.6,"n":"Dinita Stonemantle","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8999":{"id":8999,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Deliana your Wildheart Cowl and Wildheart Vest.\nWildheart Cowl Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nWildheart Vest General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"That's an amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved. Now maybe I'll be able to sleep at night with both eyes shut.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you'll really enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nFeralheart Cowl Feralheart Vest\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Wildheart pieces in exchange for your new Feralheart Cowl and Vest?","done":"I'm going to miss you, ‹name›. I owe you such a debt of gratitude; I think I'll never be able to repay it.\nI hope that you enjoy your new head and chest armor, and that it protects you for a long time to come.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"199":{"id":199,"t":"A Dark Threat Looms","lv":18,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Chief Engineer Hinderweir and show him the clue that you discovered.\nStrange Smelling Powder\nProvided: Strange Smelling Powder","desc":"You take a sample of the strange smelling powder.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Did you happen to discover any clues, ‹name›?","done":"This is an alarming discovery, to say the least!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":56.1,"y":13.2,"n":"Suspicious Barrel","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":46,"y":13.6,"n":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8679":{"id":8679,"t":"Grimtotem the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":76.7,"y":37.9,"n":"Elder Grimtotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1879":{"id":1879,"t":"Speak with Bink","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Bink in Ironforge.","desc":"‹name›! Bink, my gnome colleague in Ironforge, sends word. She has a task that needs doing and won't rely on anyone but a mage to do it! Are you that mage, ‹name›?\nIf so, then speak with Bink. She spends her time in the Hall of Mysteries in the Mystic Ward of Ironforge.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Oh, I can see you have promise, yes you do! But it takes more than promise to be a good mage. And if you're not a good mage, then you're a bad mage. And bad mages are part of the problem, yes they are!\nOops, I'm getting ahead of things. Let's begin at the start!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.5,"y":52.1,"n":"Magis Sparkmantle","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":22.4,"n":"Bink","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"1959":{"id":1959,"t":"Report to Anastasia","lv":15,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Anastasia Hartwell.","desc":"The mages of the Undercity have noted a magical disturbance within the city, and have sent word for mages of the Horde to investigate.\nAnastasia Hartwell can tell you more. Speak with her in the Magic Quarter in the Undercity.","rew":"Experience: 110","done":"It is true. A magical disturbance has been detected in our city. We are not yet sure of its origin, or whether it is malign or benign. We must first gather more information...\nAnd that, ‹name›, brings us to your task.\nOrgrimmar Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":39.2,"y":86.3,"n":"Uthel'nay","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":10,"n":"Anastasia Hartwell","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9319":{"id":9319,"t":"A Light in Dark Places","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and touch the bonfires located within Blackrock Spire, Dire Maul, Scholomance, and Stratholme, then return to the Festival Flamekeeper.\nFlame of Dire Maul\nFlame of Blackrock Spire\nFlame of Stratholme in Stratholme\nFlame of the Scholomance in Scholomance","desc":"We are not the only ones who celebrate this holiday, ‹name›. All creatures, all cultures, are touched by the flame. Even in the darkest places, the fires are being lit.\nIf you wish to see them for yourself, travel into the depths. Seek out the bonfires burning within Stratholme, Scholomance, among the ogres of Dire Maul, and the halls of Blackrock Spire itself; I will await your return.","rew":"You will receive:\nCaptured Flame 10 Burning Blossom\nExperience: 4,950","back":"Have you found your way through the dark?","done":"You have proven that you are not entirely useless, mortal.\nOrgrimmar Tirisfal Glades Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.6,"y":34.2,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.6,"y":91.9,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"99079":{"id":99079,"t":"Longwalker malah","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Longwalker Malah Longwind east of Bloodhoof Village, near the edge of Mulgore.","desc":"The Longwalkers are our people's most trusted scouts. Though their loyalty lies with the High Chieftain alone, young Baine at times seeks their aid.\nThis is one such time. Longwalker Malah was dispatched near our borders to the east and did not return last night after three days. When this occurs, it is our duty to confirm their safety.\nI must ensure the village remains safe. Prove yourself, and seek Malah out. You will know her by her headband and feathered staff, emblematic of the Longwalkers.","done":"It is clear that Malah did not die naturally. Arrows cover her back and the ground nearby.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.6,"y":63,"n":"Brave Wildrunner","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":57.6,"y":63.2,"n":"Malah Longwind","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"759":{"id":759,"t":"Wildmane Totem","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Prairie Alpha Teeth to Mull Thunderhorn in Bloodhoof Village.\n8 Prairie Alpha Tooth Prairie Wolf Alpha 36 %","desc":"There is but one water well left to cleanse, named after the Wildmane clan. For this well to be pure, the land must offer the teeth of a fierce predator, the prairie wolf alpha. Find the alphas to the north, then return to me when your hunt is finished.\nAlphas often wander around the base of our mighty city, Thunder Bluff.","rew":"Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"‹name›. Do you have the teeth I asked for?","done":"Very good, ‹name›. I can feel the sacrifice of the land in this offering, and my spirit swells with sadness, and pride.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.5,"y":63.6,"n":"Mull Thunderhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9079":{"id":9079,"t":"Bonescythe Helmet","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -75g instead of 0.","obj":"Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Bonescythe Helmet if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Helmet, 15 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 8 Cured Rugged Hides, 1 Nexus Crystal and 75 gold pieces.\nDesecrated Helmet\n15 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n8 Cured Rugged Hide\nNexus Crystal","desc":"If you want Bonescythe made, you're going to have to supply the materials.\nEnter Naxxramas, the big floating city of death in the sky up there, and find desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps. Bring those back along with the materials to put everything together and you'll have your Bonescythe. Oh, and you'll need to pay me for my troubles... I'll supply the bones.","rew":"You will receive:\nBonescythe Helmet\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n,you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Bonescythe Helmet.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9239":{"id":9239,"t":"Glacial Gloves","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -200g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 4 Essences of Water, 2 Ironweb Spider Silks and 200 gold.\n5 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n4 Bolt of Runecloth Felsteel Chest 0.9 % , Twilight Lord Everun 0 %\n4 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n2 Ironweb Spider Silk Mother Smolderweb 50 % , Crystal Fang 47 % , Gretheer 16.2 % , Plague Lurker 13.9 % and 4 more","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion, may he rest in peace, I am now able to create Glacial gloves. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nGlacial Gloves","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8919":{"id":8919,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Dreadmist Bracers to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\n15 Silithus Venom Sample Stonelash Scorpid 30 % , Stonelash Pincer 30 % , Stonelash Flayer 30 % , Sand Skitterer 30 % and 1 more\nDreadmist Bracers Summoned Blackhand Dreadweaver 3.5 % , Blackhand Dreadweaver 3.4 % , Smolderthorn Seer 2 % , Firebrand Dreadweaver 1.8 % and 3 more","desc":"Hail, ‹class›! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.\nPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.\nI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathmist Bracers\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you obtained the items I require, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes. Mux will be quite happy with this.\nThose bracers were part of a larger armor set. If you're interested in providing me with further assistance, I'd be willing to consider parting with the rest of it.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"2999":{"id":2999,"t":"Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge","desc":"Hello, ‹name›. I know you're busy helping out the people of Dun Morogh, but when you have the time, you should go upstairs and speak to one of our most respected ilk: Tiza Battleforge. She's the one the younger paladins go to when it's time they learn more about the Light and what's expected of ya.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"Well met, ‹name›. I hope the Light shows you the true path and keeps you safe from evil.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.8,"y":22.1,"n":"Brandur Ironhammer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7639":{"id":7639,"t":"To Show Due Judgment","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Exorcism Censer to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.\nRohan's Exorcism Censer\nProvided: Rohan's Exorcism Censer","desc":"With my blessings, take the censer. I myself have used it in several exorcisms, and it should serve you well for the arduous tasks that lie ahead.\nReturn now to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind, ‹name›. Your quest continues with him.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Welcome back, ‹name›. Have you acquired the exorcism censer?","done":"Yes, this will do. You will be called upon more than once during this process to make acts of sacrifice; I am glad to see that you are willing to do just that. Sacrifice is a key component in what it takes to uphold the duties of being a Paladin... but I don't have to lecture you on that.\nNow ‹name›, you will need to show due judgment in your actions. To that end, this censer will act as your vessel to dispense such judgment on tortured spirits of lands lost to us.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.4,"n":"High Priest Rohan","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5639":{"id":5639,"t":"Desperate Prayer","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","rew":"You will learn: Desperate Prayer\nExperience: 210","done":"I'm glad you've arrived, ‹name›. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.\nThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we'll begin discussing some of those now.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.4,"n":"High Priest Rohan","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"119":{"id":119,"t":"Return to Verner","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Verner Osgood in Redridge. Give him the Crate of Horseshoes.\nCrate of Horseshoes\nProvided: Crate of Horseshoes","desc":"Ok, I'll give him his 50 horseshoes...\nHere they are, all boxed up and ready to go! Tell Verner it was a pleasure doing business, and be sure he reads the note attached to this crate!","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 675\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Great, you're back! Did you get the shoes?","done":"Thank you, this really helps me out.\nBut what's this? Argus sent a note with the crate...What?? Argus wants me to PAY him? Bah!\nWell, ‹name›, thank you for your help.\nElwynn Forest Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.7,"y":65.5,"n":"Smith Argus","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":25.9,"y":47.3,"n":"Verner Osgood","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8839":{"id":8839,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with the Gnomeregan exiles. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":28.5,"n":"Officer Porterhouse","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"2359":{"id":2359,"t":"Klaven's Tower","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Steal the Defias Tower Key, break into the Defias Tower and uncover the contents of the Duskwood Chest. Take whatever information you find back to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind. Read Kearnen's Journal to gain insight about the tower.\nKlaven Mortwake's Journal Duskwood Chest\nDefias Tower Key Malformed Defias Drone\nProvided: Kearnen's Journal","desc":"I've been staking out this tower for weeks, ‹name›. Recently a major shipment came through from Duskwood, and along with it came those guards.\nWhat are they? Your guess is as good as mine. I can tell you one thing - they aren't human.\nAnyhow, the shipment had a chest - which is what I assume those abominations are guarding. The zombie with the spikes holds a key we'll need.\nGet that key, get in the tower, and uncover whatever is in that chest. Take your findings back to Mathias.","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Thistle Tea\nYou will learn: Poisons\nExperience: 1,950","back":"Any news from Agent Kearnen?","done":"This would explain the Defias drones you and Kearnen saw outside of the tower, ‹name›. It would also explain the Venture Company's involvement with the Defias and the strange shipments out of Duskwood.\nAccording to this book, the Zanzil trolls in Stranglethorn have discovered a way to raise the dead through potions... or to be more specific: poison.\nYou'll be of no use to SI:7 without a firm understanding of poisons, ‹name› -- especially with the recipe to create undeath at our fingertips.\nWestfall Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":68.5,"y":70.1,"n":"Agent Kearnen","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"8359":{"id":8359,"t":"Flexing for Nougat","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Do a flex emote at Innkeeper Gryshka, and in exchange you'll receive Orgrimmar Nougat!","desc":"That's an... interesting costume you have on. Even though you're being nice and helping a sick child trick-or-treat this year, I'm afraid I'm going to have to ask you perform a trick for me!\nLet's see... you look so strong and buff in that... costume... let's see you flex! Yes, go on now and flex for me, strong man/woman!\nWhen and only when you flex, I'll give you some tasty Orgrimmar Nougat. It's a great Hallow's End treat.","rew":"You will receive:\nOrgrimmar Nougat","back":"No candy until you flex for me, ‹name›...","done":"You are truly mighty, haha! Well done, and thanks for being such a good sport. Here's your candy.\nHappy Hallow's End, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":54.1,"y":68.4,"n":"Innkeeper Gryshka","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8519":{"id":8519,"t":"A Pawn on the Eternal Board","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Learn all that you can of the past, then speak with Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris.","desc":"As you regain your composure and focus your gaze, you notice that something stirs within the crystal. Upon closer inspection, you realize that you are looking into the past... a memory... long forgotten.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"After Staghelm's betrayal, I gathered the shattered pieces of the Scepter of the Shifting Sands and returned here. I had every intention of protecting the scepter from those that would seek to use it to cause harm to our world - thus was born the charge of the Dragonflights.\nA scepter divided amongst the four mighty Aspects would prove to be nearly impossible to restore for those willfully seeking chaos... or so I thought. What a fool I was. Even now I am hunted by that cursed flight.\nSilithus Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":28.7,"y":89.1,"n":"Crystalline Tear","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8279":{"id":8279,"t":"The Twilight Lexicon","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the three chapters of the Twilight Lexicon to Hermit Ortell in Silithus.\nTwilight Lexicon - Chapter 1 Twilight Keeper Mayna\nTwilight Lexicon - Chapter 2 Twilight Keeper Exeter\nTwilight Lexicon - Chapter 3 Twilight Keeper Havunth","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer are not kind to those that leave their ranks. They hunt me to this day like I'm some sort of beast! Needless to say, an enemy of theirs is a friend of mine!\nTo decipher this Tablet I'll need the book used by their scribes to encode secret messages: the Twilight Lexicon. It's such an important tool that they keep its three chapters in different locations! The officers entrusted with the Lexicon are known as Twilight Keepers, look for them at the Twilight's Hammer camps.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Who goes there? Oh, it's you! Did you find all the Lexicon chapters yet?","done":"Yes! These are the parts to the book! Let's get started then, ‹name›.\nSwap every third word with words from the second chapter... then swap every other word with words from the first chapter... Wait, did I get that backwards?","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":67.2,"y":69.8,"n":"Hermit Ortell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"439":{"id":439,"t":"Rot Hide Clues","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Deliah's Ring to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.\nDeliah's Ring\nProvided: Deliah's Ring","desc":"Among the corpses a hand protrudes, unwrapped. It is the hand of a woman, pockmarked from the plague but relatively fresh.\nOn the hand is a ring. Removing the ring and inspecting it reveals an engraving:\n\"For Deliah\"","rew":"Experience: 290\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"‹name›. You return, so I assume your investigations bore fruit?","done":"You say that this ring was worn by a woman, recently killed?\nThe only nearby source of such a body would be the mass graves in Tirisfal. The Rot Hide Gnolls must be taking those corpses to Fenris Isle!","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":58.4,"y":34.9,"n":"Corpse Laden Boat","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1479":{"id":1479,"t":"The Bough of the Eternals","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the orphan to the bank of Darnassus. The bank itself is hollowed out of a tree known as the Bough of the Eternals.","desc":"I've heard stories about how the night elves have their bank in a tree - one that looks like a bear! That's so cool! Night elves are neat how they like nature and stuff, but bears are just totally awesome!\nWould you take me to see the bear-tree in Darnassus, please? There's a boat that will take us close to there, and it shouldn't take very long. Please, please, please!","rew":"Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Alliance","back":"Are we there yet?","done":"Wow, it was cooler than I even imagined - the Bough of the Eternals! I didn't think it'd be so big, but it was! Did you see the bird on top of it too?! I wonder how they got the branches to look like that!\nThanks for taking me to Darnassus, ‹name›. You're awesome!\nDarnassus Open the zone on the world map Start Human Orphan End Human Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Alliance Shareable No Quest ID 1479\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 650 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Children's Week\nUse the Human Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\nOrphan Matron Nightingale Stormwind City\n2 [ 60 ] The Bough of the Eternals this quest\nTake the orphan to the bank of Darnassus.\nHuman Orphan\n650 XP","cats":["special"]},"1079":{"id":1079,"t":"Covert Ops - Alpha","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Venture Co.'s Engineering Plans from the lumber mill in Windshear Crag.\nVenture Co. Engineering Plans Venture Co. Engineering Plans\nProvided: Covert Ops Pack","desc":"This is it, ‹name›. Pay close attention. The devices are done, and ready to be used.\nTake these pages--they'll explain more about the detonators and explosives, and where you should place them.\nRemember, the success of your mission doesn't depend on how much destruction you cause. Plan Alpha's success depends on you bringing back the Venture Co.'s engineering plans from inside the lumber mill south of Cragpool Lake.","rew":"Experience: 2,200\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Did you get the plans, ‹name›?","done":"Truly amazing! This is a huge blow to the Venture Co.\nWe'll be able to find weaknesses in their machines and also incorporate their designs into our own creations. This is a wonderful day, indeed.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"599":{"id":599,"t":"The Bloodsail Buccaneers","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report the planned Bloodsail attack to Fleet Master Seahorn.","desc":"Shiver me timbers! So the Bloodsail Buccaneers are planning some sort of attack on Booty Bay? Why, the nerve of those scoundrels. Booty Bay will always be run by the Blackwater Raiders!\nThis is bigger than I thought. Report what you have learned to Fleet Master Seahorn at once! The ol' sea dog is around town somewhere....","rew":"Experience: 825\n+25 reputation with Booty Bay\n-125 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"Bloodsail Buccaneers attacking Booty Bay? They might as well throw themselves off the Overlook Cliffs. Nonetheless, by bringing me this information you have done my fleet of swashbucklers a great service. The Blackwater Raiders thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.1,"y":76.2,"n":"First Mate Crazz","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":77,"n":"Fleet Master Seahorn","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8599":{"id":8599,"t":"Love Song for Narain","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Meridith's Love Letter to Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris.\nMeridith's Love Letter\nProvided: Meridith's Love Letter","desc":"It isn't often that I get visitors. As a matter of fact, the last time I had a visitor was when I rescued that dear, sweet gnome from the wreckage of the crashed flying machine.\n<Meridith gazes into nothingness, lost in a memory.>\nDo you know him? Narain? Narain Soothfancy? Oh it would mean so much to me if somebody would deliver a message to him for me. I must tell him how I feel! I know it's love! I just know it!\nCould you possibly deliver a message to Narain? I would be forever indebted to you!","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+10 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You smell like fish!","done":"What!?\n<Narain starts to fidget.>\nWell, um... What do you want me to do??? She's a fish! A FISH I tell you! And I'm a gnome. It could never work out.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":59.4,"y":96,"n":"Meridith the Mermaiden","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8759":{"id":8759,"t":"The Path of the Invoker","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You honor my kind, ‹name›. Strike down the enemies of Kalimdor! Show them what it means to deface the land of eternal starlight.\nYou have earned another enhancement. Hand me your signet ring so that I may bolster its power.","done":"Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, ‹name›. May you never stray from the path of the invoker!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"919":{"id":919,"t":"Timberling Sprouts","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Timberling Sprouts to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.\n12 Timberling Sprout Timberling Sprout","desc":"Small timberlings are sprouting around the waters of Lake Al'Ameth. I'm afraid these sprouts are beyond help -- we should try to clear them from the land before they grow large enough to cause trouble.\nWhen you're wandering the lake, if you see any timberling sprouts please take them. Help keep our land clean!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGardening Gloves Graystone Bracers\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 800\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Have you found any sprouts near the waters?","done":"That's a lot! I'm afraid they're spreading at a dangerous rate. I hope I can solve the riddle of what is tainting them.\nThank you for your help, ‹name›. The land is a cleaner place from your efforts.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"1159":{"id":1159,"t":"Test of Lore","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,200 experience instead of 950, 1.26 times as much.","obj":"Find Parqual Fintallas in Undercity.","desc":"Well done, ‹name›. You have passed the first portion of the Test of Lore, but there is still another question to be answered. But that question is not mine to ask.\nSeek out Parqual Fintallas in Lordaeron City. He was a great historian for the humans before the Plague overtook him. Now he continues to seek enlightenment, but of a different nature.\nHe will have another requirement of you before he asks you anything, but you have done masterfully thus far--I'm sure you will overcome his obstacle.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"Braug sent you? Impossible.\n<Parqual looks you up and down.>\nBraved Dor'Danil, took a leap of faith, fought and overpowered a powerful elemental? Bah! You're probably a farce; some adventurer that overheard talk in a tavern. And now you think you have what it takes to pass my test. So be it... ‹class›.\nStonetalon Mountains Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":78.8,"y":45.7,"n":"Braug Dimspirit","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":57.8,"y":65.4,"n":"Parqual Fintallas","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"359":{"id":359,"t":"Forsaken Duties","lv":9,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Deathguard Linnea.","desc":"I need a fresh report from our Deathguard waystation to the east.\nI must know if more Scourge forces have slipped past The Bulwark and into Tirisfal. Our vigilance on the border to the Plaguelands must be maintained - we can't let the Scourge get a stronger foothold here!\nTravel south along the road, then east at the fork to the waystation. Speak with Deathguard Linnea. She has the information I need.","rew":"Experience: 200\n+25 reputation with Undercity","done":"Magistrate Sevren wants a report? Very well: the defenders at The Bulwark are holding the majority of the Scourge at bay, but some do slip through on occasion.\nWe have seen sporadic Scourge activity east of this station, with a concentration around the Balnir Farmstead.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.3,"y":50.8,"n":"Magistrate Sevren","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.5,"y":60.3,"n":"Deathguard Linnea","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2199":{"id":2199,"t":"Lore for a Price","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring five silver bars to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.\n5 Silver Bar Tattered Chest 9 % , Battered Chest 9 % , Tattered Chest 3 % , Battered Chest 0 % and 4 more","desc":"I am a jeweler of great renown here in Ironforge! Well, former renown anyway... I have fallen onto hard times due to the chicanery of a competitor! A bad reputation in this business spells financial disaster. As a result, I find myself without a copper to my good-though-currently-sullied name.\nI want you to get me five silver bars to finish an order I received - the first in what seems like an eternity.\nYou get me those five silver bars, and I'll answer your questions on the necklace.","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Have you got the five silver bars I asked for? I will share my sad tale of woe with you concerning the necklace you now possess... but only after I get those bars! Please, help a gnome out, won't ya?","done":"You're all right in my book; I don't care what everyone else has been saying... I kid, I kid! Seriously, thank you my friend.\nNow, the necklace you have is one of my finest creations, but it is missing three gems that help bind magic power to it. I crafted it for a paladin some time ago. He was on a self-appointed quest to clear out the \"evil taint\" present at an excavation site in the Badlands called Uldaman.\nWell... that paladin died in Uldaman, and that was just the beginning of my woes.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Talvash del Kissel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"2279":{"id":2279,"t":"The Platinum Discs","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the miniature version of the Discs of Norgannon to the Explorers' League in Ironforge.\nMiniature Platinum Discs\nProvided: Miniature Platinum Discs","desc":"Touching the Discs of Norgannon once again makes your hand tingle. This time, however, a strange grinding noise is heard from inside the discs.\nYour backpack suddenly becomes heavier than it was before. Inside, you discover a miniature version of the discs!\nNo doubt, an item of this sort would be invaluable for someone interested in the ancient history of Azeroth. The Explorers' League in Ironforge is such a group, known throughout the Alliance; perhaps they can make good use of it.","rew":"Experience: 5,250\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Yes, may I help you with something? I assure you I am a very busy right now. If it is grave importance to the Explorers' League, however, then I am all ears!","done":"What do you have there... oh my. You found this where?\nNo, really?\nYou spoke to whom about what?\nNO, REALLY?!\nMy fine ‹class›, you may have just made the archaeological find of the year! By the Gods who am I kidding, the find of the century! If these discs are what I think them to be, then this could be the very key we have been looking for! This may well prove outright once and for all the legitimacy of the Dwarves' enchanted creation!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":24.1,"n":"High Explorer Magellas","e":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"999":{"id":999,"t":"When dreams turn to nightmares","lv":25,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Level 25 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 21 23 28 33 Side Both factions Type Elite Shareable Yes Quest ID 999","cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"1799":{"id":1799,"t":"Fragments of the Orb of Orahil","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Menara's acolytes inside the tower above Ratchet and choose one of their paths to follow.\nAfterwards, bring an Infernal Orb to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\nInfernal Orb Burning Blade Summoner 55 %","desc":"Good, then we shall begin.\nThe first thing you must do is speak to my acolytes inside. Choose one of their paths to follow--they will explain more.\nSecond, you must travel to Desolace and find an Infernal Orb from one of the warlocks of Mannoroc Coven. It is that orb that you will cleanse with the help of a mage named Tabetha deep in southern Dustwallow Marsh. She will aid you because of our history together.\nAgain, do not come back until you have done both things I've asked.","rew":"Experience: 3,150","back":"And obviously not being a mage, I wonder if I can trust you at all. I can smell the power of the arcane on you, but you seem to have eluded the stank of corruption that comes so willingly with your kind.\nYes, a warlock... a warlock has come to ask for my help.\nWell, what is it I can do for you, ‹name›?","done":"Oh, so Menara sent you. Fair enough... I suppose you may stay as my guest for the time being. But you must be on some pressing business - perhaps you're here seeking lost power? Maybe I'm mistaken. Maybe corruption isn't too far away from you after all.\nThe Barrens Dustwallow Marsh Desolace","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1639":{"id":1639,"t":"Bartleby the Drunk","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Bartleby.","desc":"Yeah, I can teach you. But first I wanna see what moves you have already.\nSee that drunk over there at the end of the bar? Bartleby? I want you to get his mug.\nHah, and if you know Bartleby then you know he won't just give it to you.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Hello, fancy boy/girl! What's a prissy thing like you doing in the Pig and Whistle? Be careful, or you might break a nail...","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.1,"y":53.3,"n":"Harry Burlguard","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":76.8,"y":52.5,"n":"Bartleby","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1719":{"id":1719,"t":"The Affray","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Big Will, then speak to Klannoc Macleod on Fray Island.\nBig Will slain","desc":"If you want to learn from me, then you must first pass The Affray. It is a challenge we on Fray Island like to offer rising warriors who think they're tough, and if you can pass this test then I'll know you are.\nTo begin, walk into the middle of that crowd yonder and step on the grate. That'll tell Twiggy Flathead you're ready, and he'll send challengers against you.\nBeat all the challengers and he'll call out Big Will. Kill Big Will, and return to me in the time we allow.","rew":"Experience: 2,450","back":"Have you completed your challenge?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. You have passed The Affray!\nYou are a worthy warrior, and I am honored to teach you...\nThe Barrens Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":68.6,"y":49.2,"n":"Klannoc Macleod","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"279":{"id":279,"t":"Claws from the Deep","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Bluegill Murlocs.\nSlay Gobbler and take his head.\nBring Gobbler's Head to Karl Boran in Menethil Harbor.\nGobbler's Head Gobbler\nBluegill Murloc slain : 0/ 12","desc":"Murlocs are crawling out from the deep waters and building their villages on the coastline. They are harassing our fishers and merchants and must be stopped.\nOne of these murlocs, Gobbler, skulks with other bluegill murlocs and harries merchants along the road, always then retreating to the safety of the nearby murloc hovels. Our merchants are in jeopardy, and we will pay to secure them.\nGobbler prowls the river inlet north of here. Find him, slay his kin, and bring me his head.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Our merchants will not be safe until we are rid of Gobbler and those Murlocs.","done":"Ah, well done ‹name›.\nAccept this as payment for fulfillment of your contract with the Merchant Marines.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.3,"y":58.6,"n":"Karl Boran","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"93319":{"id":93319,"t":"Pilfered windstones","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 Pilfered Windstones from the Highlands Bandits in the Shen'dar Highlands.\n10 Pilfered Windstone","desc":"We are relying on windstones more and more for day to day living here on Zephras so we try and maintain a cache of them in reserve for emergencies. Lately I've noticed some go missing from our stores.\nWe've found windstones on bandits we've captured recently, and I suspect they are behind our shortages.\nIf you find yourself near the bandit cave to the north, mind knocking a few heads together and reclaiming some of our pilfered windstones for me?","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 480\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"These sneakthieves have likely been breaking into our supplies for months. I tried to convince Aonda to put a raid together to clear out that bandit cave for good, but she didn't want to pull the few peacekeepers we have away from the village.\nWith the cultists at Falaath Village to the south growing in numbers, I suppose I can't fault her for that.","done":"Thanks ‹class›. This should help us get by for now. If we can't get the supply routes squared away soon though, a few stolen windstones will be the least of our worries.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.4,"y":45,"n":"Teeri Wellwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92679":{"id":92679,"t":"Blood tithe","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Listen to what Alvarion Windfield has to say and find Aamelia Windfield at the Windfield Orchard.\nFind Aamelia Windfield\nListen to Alvarion Windfield's Story","desc":"H--Hello, stranger. You have the look of a capable adventurer about you. I...\n<The Skyborne man winces, clearly suffering terrible pain>\n...I was wondering if you were seeking employment? I came here to Valanaar to recruit fighters to help save my farm. If you are interested, please go find my wife Aamelia Windfield at our orchard to the west of Valanaar, in the lowlands.","back":"What? Alvarion is alive?","done":"<Aamelia listens while you explain what became of Alvarion.>\nAt least I know he's going to be safe in Valanaar.\nStranger, I hate to tell you this but I think my idiot husband likely just sent you here to die for nothing. If you have any sense at all, you should leave now. This isn't your fight.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":62,"y":73.2,"n":"Alvarion Windfield","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.6,"y":81.8,"n":"Aamelia Windfield","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93159":{"id":93159,"t":"The strange hermit","lv":13,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with the Strange Hermit in the Shadowgale Forest and learn more about him.\nLearn more about the Strange Hermit","desc":"Uh, um... h-hello, I mean to say, hi! Greetings, even! I'm sorry... its um, been so long since I've actually spoken to another person. I'm afraid I'm a bit rusty at this.\n<The strange hooded figure shifts uncomfortably before you.>\nSo er, um... how is your day going?","back":"So that's the story...","done":"...that's about all I have to say about it. I was--um--somewhere else before I was here. Now I'm here and I have my friends, and my things. T-things I built, I mean. That's about all I need. I think that's all I need, anyway.\nI have to say though, it is nice to talk to someone who will talk back. The forest spirits try, but they just end up singing at me. That's nice in its own way, but not exactly s-stimulating conversation.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":54,"y":39,"n":"Strange Hermit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8119":{"id":8119,"t":"The Unmarred Vision of Voodress","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Vision of Voodress","rew":"You will receive:\nUnmarred Vision of Voodress\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"<Maywiki points to your talisman.>\nLook at it, ‹name›! It's come alive. The spirits dance around the orb.\nGive it to Maywiki so she can make one last adjustment.","done":"One day, ‹name›, you will be able to use this orb to communicate directly with me. Whenever this battle with Hakkar be over and Maywiki go home. Let us call to the spirits and ask them for that day to come soon.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});